I wonder if you really don't get this.

Scorched earth has a much simpler concept, not a lot of game depth,
but nevertheless is fun to play, especially in multiplayer.

It's much easier to get such a game a visual make over, adding network
support or whatever.

This is completely different from NetHack. Evolving the gameplay is
part of variants like Slash'Em, SporkHack and UnNetHack. But
nevertheless NetHack has a lots of GUI frontends that are modern, for
example Vulture or the iPhone (you can't get more modern than that).

